<header class="mb-6">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-display">Operator</h1>
  <p class="text-foreground/70">
    Every tool that runs the clinic — the rules, the process, the discovery,
    and the helper agent.
  </p>
</header>

<% section_chip =
  "mr-2 inline-block size-3.5 -rotate-6 rounded-base border-2 border-border" %>

<%!-- Operations index: every operational surface as a first-class link,
      above the prose sections — the hub used to bury /operator/rules,
      /operator/tasks and the diagram tools inside content cards, which
      read exactly like the links were missing. One row each: where, and
      why you'd go. --%>
<%!-- CLIN-5: the grid duplicated the cards in the sections below, so it
      now folds — collapsed by default, native <details>, the Day view's
      Earlier-today pattern (free keyboard access, no JS). --%>
<section class="mb-8" data-testid="operations-index">
  <details
    data-testid="operations-index-details"
    class="rounded-base border-2 border-border bg-secondary-background px-4 py-3 shadow-shadow"
  >
    <summary class="cursor-pointer font-heading">
      <span class={section_chip <> " bg-yellow"} aria-hidden="true" />Operations index
      <span class="ml-2 text-sm font-base text-foreground/60">
        every surface, one click away
      </span>
    </summary>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <.card accent="yellow" href="/operator/rules">
        <h3 class="font-heading">Rules</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          Author compliance rules and walk a bundle through draft, validate,
          approve, activate, compile.
        </p>
      </.card>
      <.card accent="yellow" href="/operator/tasks">
        <h3 class="font-heading">Tasks</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          The engine's task inbox for the acting clinician — claim, complete,
          delegate.
        </p>
      </.card>
      <.card accent="yellow" href="/operator/processes/appointment_visit/designer">
        <h3 class="font-heading">Process designer</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          Draw and publish the visit process: catalogue-backed action and
          decision refs as comboboxes.
        </p>
      </.card>
      <.card accent="yellow" href="/operator/decisions/appointment.triage/editor">
        <h3 class="font-heading">DMN editor</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          Edit and publish the triage decision table; a changed rule takes
          effect on the next booking.
        </p>
      </.card>
      <.card accent="yellow" href="#recent-instances">
        <h3 class="font-heading">Recent instances</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          The latest visit instances below — each opens in the token viewer.
        </p>
      </.card>
      <.card accent="yellow" href="/events">
        <h3 class="font-heading">Events</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          The audit event log, newest first. Read-only by construction.
        </p>
      </.card>
      <.card accent="yellow" href="/evaluations">
        <h3 class="font-heading">Evaluations</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          Decision evidence: which version of which table decided, and why.
        </p>
      </.card>
      <.card accent="yellow" href="/dev/dashboard">
        <h3 class="font-heading">LiveDashboard</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          Request timings, the process tree, VM and telemetry metrics.
        </p>
      </.card>
      <.card accent="yellow" href="/agent">
        <h3 class="font-heading">Agent console</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          Ask about the clinic's data, or ask for a composed surface on the
          fly.
        </p>
      </.card>
      <.card accent="yellow" href="/canvas">
        <h3 class="font-heading">Canvas</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          The domain as a navigable graph — domains, resources,
          relationships.
        </p>
      </.card>
      <.card accent="yellow" href="/emergencies">
        <h3 class="font-heading">Emergency board</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          The emergency triage lane — severity-5 bookings and the alert path.
        </p>
      </.card>
      <.card accent="yellow" href="/operator/surfaces">
        <h3 class="font-heading">Surface editor</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          Browse, edit, preview, export — the declared surfaces as dynamic
          specs, validated live.
        </p>
      </.card>
      <.card accent="yellow" href="http://docke:8444">
        <h3 class="font-heading">Development IDE</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          VS Code in the browser, mounted on this repo: ElixirLS, the docker
          gates, opencode in the terminal. Tailnet (password in .dev-access).
        </p>
      </.card>
    </div>
    <p
      class="mt-3 text-xs text-foreground/60"
      title="Oban runs with an inline config and an empty queue in this demo, so there is no jobs dashboard to link."
    >
      Oban is configured inline with an empty queue in this demo — no jobs
      dashboard to link.
    </p>
  </details>
</section>

<%!-- CLIN-6: the capstone deck, presentable from this page during a demo.
      NOT inside the collapsed index above — presenting is the one flow that
      must be one click from the page's top. The slideshow is the static
      /deck route; the pptx is the same deck as a download. --%>
<section class="mb-8" data-testid="deck-links">
  <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <.card accent="yellow" href="/deck">
      <h3 class="font-heading">The deck — present the walkthrough</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        The capstone slideshow: twelve slides, arrow keys to move, same
        neobrutalist tokens as the app. Starts at the thesis, ends at the
        live-demo script.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="yellow" href="/deck/capstone-deck.pptx" download="capstone-deck.pptx">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Deck download (.pptx)</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        The same deck as a PowerPoint file, for presenting it anywhere.
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</section>

<%!-- Each section owns one accent color (chip in the heading, dotted strip
      on its cards, colored lift-shadow on hover). The accents give the hub
      a scavenger-hunt readability: you find the section by its color before
      you read a word. Cards are the shared <.card> recipe; the palette is
      the accent, never the fill — bodies stay white, borders stay black. --%>
<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class={section_chip <> " bg-violet"} aria-hidden="true" />Rules &amp; process
  </h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <.card accent="violet" href="/operator/decisions/appointment.triage/editor">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Decision table editor</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Edit and publish the triage table. A changed rule takes effect on
        the next booking — no deploy.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="violet" href="/operator/processes/appointment_visit/designer">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Process designer</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Draw the visit process: triage, check-in, the consult, labs,
        discharge. Publish a new version of the graph.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="violet" href="/decisions">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Published rules</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Which version of each decision table and process is live, and what
        came before.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="violet" href="/processes">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Published processes</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">The visit processes, versioned.</p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="violet" href="/worklist">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Timers &amp; escalations</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Escalation timers ride the tasks themselves — the four-hour lab
        wait shows as a due date here. The engine ships no separate
        trigger UI.
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class={section_chip <> " bg-orange"} aria-hidden="true" />Work
  </h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <.card accent="orange" href="/operator/tasks">
      <h3 class="font-heading">My tasks</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        The engine's own inbox for the acting clinician — claim, complete,
        delegate.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="orange" href="/worklist">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Worklist</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Every open task in one board, completed through the engine so the
        token advances.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="orange" href="/visits">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Visit processes</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Where each visit stands; open one's instance viewer for the token
        overlay on the graph.
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</section>

<%!-- The lifecycle as a formal machine, rendered from its declaration
      (AshStateMachine.Charts — derived from the resource, so it cannot
      drift from it). The <pre> is the no-JS fallback; operator_diagram.js
      replaces it with the SVG. A live diagram inside Clarity is a queued
      follow-up. --%>
<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class={section_chip <> " bg-orange"} aria-hidden="true" />Visit state machine
  </h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <%!-- The lifecycle as a formal machine, rendered from its
             declaration (AshStateMachine.Charts — derived from the
             resource, so it cannot drift from it). The <pre> is the no-JS
             fallback; operator_diagram.js replaces it with the SVG. A live
             diagram inside Clarity is a queued follow-up. --%>
    <.card accent="orange" class="overflow-x-auto lg:col-span-2">
      <h3 class="font-heading">The lifecycle, as declared</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        One authority on which status moves a visit may make — the
        resource's own state machine. The process graph decides when to
        ask for a move; this decides whether the move exists.
      </p>
      <div data-mermaid={@visit_machine_chart} class="min-w-0">
        <pre class="text-foreground/60 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap">{@visit_machine_chart}</pre>
      </div>
    </.card>
  </div>
</section>

<%!-- The diagram renderer is its own esbuild entry (mermaid is far too
     heavy for app.js, which every page loads) — loaded by this page
     alone. --%>
<script defer phx-track-static type="text/javascript" src={~p"/assets/js/operator_diagram.js"}>
</script>

<%!-- The Visits surface can't link a row to its instance viewer (the a2ui
     surface DSL has no external row links), so this list is the bridge:
     latest instances, each a link into /operator/instances/:id. --%>
<section class="mb-8" id="recent-instances">
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class={section_chip <> " bg-main"} aria-hidden="true" />Recent visit processes
  </h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <%= for instance <- @recent_instances do %>
      <.card accent="main" href={"/operator/instances/#{instance.id}"}>
        <h3 class="font-heading">{instance.subject_label}</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          Standing at <span class="font-medium">{instance.current_node}</span>
          · status {instance.status}{if instance.outcome, do: " · outcome #{instance.outcome}"}
        </p>
      </.card>
    <% end %>
    <%= if @recent_instances == [] do %>
      <.empty_state icon="hero-heart">
        No visit processes yet — book an appointment and one starts here.
      </.empty_state>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<%!-- Audit: what did anyone do, and what rules were they held to. The
     evaluations surface answers with decisions; the events surface with
     the raw log; the bundle card says which guard is in force right now. --%>
<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class={section_chip <> " bg-pink"} aria-hidden="true" />Audit
  </h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <.card accent="pink" href="/operator/rules">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Ruleset editor</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Author compliance rules as rows, then walk them through the
        lifecycle: draft, validate, approve, activate, compile.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="pink" href="/evaluations">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Decision evidence</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Every rule evaluation, with the matched rows — which version of
        which table decided, and why.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="pink" href="/events">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Audit events</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        The event log, newest first. Written by the event projector; the
        application only ever reads it.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="pink" href="/operator/rules">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Active guard bundle</h3>
      <%= if @active_bundle do %>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          <span class="font-mono font-medium">
            {String.slice(@active_bundle.content_hash, 0, 12)}
          </span>
          · status {@active_bundle.status}
        </p>
      <% else %>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          Nothing is in force yet — activate a bundle in the ruleset editor.
        </p>
      <% end %>
    </.card>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class={section_chip <> " bg-cyan"} aria-hidden="true" />Discovery &amp; insight
  </h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <.card accent="cyan" href="/canvas">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Data model canvas</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        The whole clinic as a navigable graph — domains, resources,
        relationships — with a surface one click from every node.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="cyan" href="/clarity">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Clarity</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Deep introspection: the module graph, ER and policy diagrams,
        supply-chain and security reports. Dev routes only.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="cyan" href="/evaluations">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Decision evidence</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Every rule evaluation, with the matched table rows — what the rule
        decided, and why.
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class={section_chip <> " bg-green"} aria-hidden="true" />Helper agent
  </h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <.card accent="green" href="/agent">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Ask &amp; compose</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Ask questions about the clinic's data, or ask for a new interface:
        the agent composes and verifies a surface on the fly and shows it
        beside the conversation. Works without an API key for browsing —
        composing needs one.
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class={section_chip <> " bg-main"} aria-hidden="true" />Infrastructure
  </h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <.card accent="main" href="/dev/dashboard">
      <h3 class="font-heading">LiveDashboard</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        The running system at a glance — request timings, the process tree,
        VM and telemetry metrics, PubSub and channel traffic.
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</section>
